guy who stole my sword.

250
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,320
I can guide you to him easily.

251
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,073
He's always at Bandit's Bridge in Ringo.

252
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:55,657
I have to get it back before the big raid.

253
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:57,920
I don't feel comfortable without it.

254
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,471
I must have really pissed off Oduchi, huh?

255
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,485
He's pulling out all the
stops to hunt us down.

256
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,040
Poor Otaku.

257
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,160
I hope she's alright.

258
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:18,370
Yasui!

259
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,120
I'm coming!

260
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:33,000
After having to witness
such a horrible scene,

261
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:35,740
I wish I'd been able to stay by her side.

262
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:39,057
You can work that out when you see her.

263
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:40,577
My friends will keep her safe.

264
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:41,719
Don't worry, okay?

265
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,880
Orji will pay for what he did.

266
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:54,980
I'll avenge Tonoyasu at any cost.

267
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:22,660
I wish I was strong, if I had the
power, I would kill him myself.

268
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:37,760
What did you say?!

269
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:42,357
You mean you let those
loathsome traitors escape?!

270
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:45,740
And what of that savage
Ronin who attacked me?!

271
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:47,670
I...

272
00:21:47,753 --> 00:21:48,980
I failed you, my lord.

273
00:21:49,380 --> 00:21:52,000
Do you have any more bad news, Will?

274
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:53,800
No, good news!

275
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,080
We captured a man named Trafalgar!

276
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:58,360
Huh? Say again?

277
00:21:58,700 --> 00:21:59,700
Trafal-what?

278
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:03,037
Who in the hell is that?!

279
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:06,677
He's an enemy intruder
just like straw had now we

280
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:09,217
have two of their masterminds
under our control.

281
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:12,220
They're helpless What
are you doing with him?

282
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:18,040
For pirates betrayal never
goes out of style right now.

283
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,080
We're putting that to use

284
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:31,500
We'll torture him first, but we'll
find other uses for him, too.

285
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:38,417
That is good news and what of the

286
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,697
capital have you quelled the riots yet?

287
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:46,057
It's all under control local
forces are on high alert samurai

288
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:49,717
and ninja are on patrol as we
speak combing every street and

289
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:53,957
establishment in town it's only a
matter of time until the intruders

290
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:59,080
are caught while we're settling
that I promise we'll keep you safe.

291
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:07,542
If you see any of these criminals,
you must report it immediately!

292
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,540
Wow, there's so many!

293
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:12,957
A lot of bad guys on the loose!

294
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:17,817
It's treason to aid them in any way, and
allowing them to escape is a crime as well!

295
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:18,840
So take heed!

296
00:23:20,220 --> 00:23:21,680
Well, that sucks.

297
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:26,684
Guess we're clearing out
of the capital for now.

298
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:29,068
We're not just wanted here.

299
00:23:29,260 --> 00:23:30,907
Now it's the entire country!

300
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:36,367
Orochi's network of assassins will be on
the lookout for us, ready for a fight.

301
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:40,344
After all, our objective was to
find allies with the Moon Tattoo.

302
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,997
Seems like kind of an
empty victory, though.

303
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:47,910
You're right.

304
00:23:47,993 --> 00:23:49,272
Unless we can free them.

305
00:23:49,660 --> 00:23:51,900
We're not criminals! Let us go!

306
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:55,900
Sit down and shut up!

307
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:59,636
I thought Toniyasu's speech
would have done the trick.

308
00:23:59,860 --> 00:24:03,137
So now they're just keeping them
locked up for the hell of it?

309
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:05,840
Well, it might be
something like that, yes?

310
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:10,097
There must be a thousand or so
rebels in the prisoners' quarters,

311
00:24:10,180 --> 00:24:12,020
suffering the whims of Orochi.

312
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:16,319
Hey, shouldn't they have
set these guys free by now?

313
00:24:16,820 --> 00:24:18,040
How would that work?

314
00:24:18,180 --> 00:24:20,400
Lord Orochi says, I goofed up?

315
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:23,942
We can't expect the Shogun
to admit he was wrong.

316
00:24:24,260 --> 00:24:25,436
That's a good point.

317
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:29,198
These people have proven
themselves to be our allies.

318
00:24:29,360 --> 00:24:33,520
We need them, and beyond
that, we owe them our aid.

319
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:37,520
Law's buddies must be
stuck in there too, huh?

320
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:40,440
Hey, Shinobu, what are those people doing?

321
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:44,540
Oh, they're preparing skyboats.

322
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:45,759
What are they for?

323
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:49,579
Skyboats are an important
part of the fire festival.

324
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:52,080
Two beloved figures just died.

325
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,317
They must not feel like celebrating.

326
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:56,860
Actually, it's just the opposite.

327
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:09,840
The Fire Festival is an event to honor
friends and family who have passed away.

328
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:16,544
And the bigger the celebration, the more
likely your thoughts will reach the dead.

329
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:18,770
I see.

330
00:25:18,853 --> 00:25:21,462
Sounds like they'd better
party pretty hard then.

331
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:35,777
You made it that's great.

332
00:25:35,860 --> 00:25:37,237
Yeah.

333
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:39,377
Sorry to worry you.

334
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:40,817
That was a real mess.

335
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:43,137
I didn't catch the details.

336
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:44,477
But I heard you got caught.

337
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,937
Luckily we escaped.

338
00:25:47,020 --> 00:25:48,377
Oh.

339
00:25:48,460 --> 00:25:49,577
All right.

340
00:25:49,660 --> 00:25:51,917
Take a look at this.

341
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,237
It's from that time.

342
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:56,120
Yasuie. Huh?

343
00:25:56,340 --> 00:25:57,420
He gave you this?

344
00:25:57,560 --> 00:26:00,857
He drew that symbol and showed
it to the people with the tattoos

345
00:26:00,940 --> 00:26:02,597
before he died. Hmm.

346
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:03,937
There's something different.

347
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:07,520
It looks like he added
two lines to the snake?

348
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:09,220
Yeah, you got it.

349
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:11,877
He changed the meaning,
but I don't know how.

350
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:13,548
Seemed to work out, though.

351
00:26:14,260 --> 00:26:17,201
What I mean is the people
from Wano understood it.

352
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:19,520
It was Yosui's final message to them.

353
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,840
This is kind of a big deal.

354
00:26:22,420 --> 00:26:23,337
I'll show Kin'emon.

355
00:26:23,420 --> 00:26:24,597
He'll know what to do.

356
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:25,937
Thank you, Nami.

357
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:27,373
Better get going, then!

358
00:26:29,120 --> 00:26:32,317
If you need help, come to
Amigasa Village, kay? Thanks.

359
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:35,224
When you see your friends,
tell them we said hi!

360
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:43,430
Captain.

361
00:26:54,700 --> 00:26:55,530
Captain!

362
00:26:55,613 --> 00:26:56,443
Captain!

363
00:26:56,600 --> 00:27:00,080
We made a bargain and
your lives were the chips.

364
00:27:00,980 --> 00:27:02,380
Our lives? What?

365
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:04,220
This sounds like a trap!

366
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:06,388
It's quite straightforward.

367
00:27:06,980 --> 00:27:11,180
If I refuse to release you, Then
your captain will take my life.

368
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,871
Which is to say, he'll take yours as well.

369
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:18,849
Never betting on tomorrow, he'll make
any sacrifice without a second thought.

370
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:22,576
I'm afraid that I must take
his threat very seriously.

371
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:25,600
Captain, I'm sorry!

372
00:27:25,940 --> 00:27:27,460
We blew it, didn't we?

373
00:27:33,340 --> 00:27:34,680
These are your lives.

374
00:27:34,820 --> 00:27:36,349
I'm returning them to you.

375
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:42,897
I hold no power over them,
and they're free to leave.

376
00:27:42,980 --> 00:27:45,686
I trust this meets your
conditions, Trafalgar.

377
00:27:50,800 --> 00:27:52,977
Our lives aren't worth it! Captain!

378
00:27:53,060 --> 00:27:53,900
Don't go!

379
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:57,420
Be quiet and listen.

380
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:02,094
Don't tell the Straw Hats I was caught.

381
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:05,360
If anyone asks questions,
just say you escaped.

382
00:28:06,340 --> 00:28:08,340
I don't get it! Captain!

383
00:28:14,340 --> 00:28:16,020
Don't do this!

384
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,460
Come back!

385
00:28:19,460 --> 00:28:22,180
It's not worth it!

386
00:28:23,220 --> 00:28:24,050
Captain!

387
00:28:31,780 --> 00:28:33,280
It's our fault!

388
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:38,380
And now, who knows what our captain
is going through with their clutches!

389
00:28:43,980 --> 00:28:46,140
We can't just sit around and wait!

390
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:49,260
As the Heart Pirates, we have a job to do!

391
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:52,305
We'll save our captain
no matter what it takes!

392
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:54,657
Kittymon's plan will have to wait!

393
00:28:54,740 --> 00:28:56,960
I will not let our captain die!

394
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:10,100
I have had enough of you, Law.

395
00:29:10,580 --> 00:29:11,780
Give it up already.

396
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:15,169
I think you need to
step away for a moment.

397
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:19,896
You've been acting out of sorts ever
since we began this interrogation.

398
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:21,030
Whatever.

399
00:29:21,113 --> 00:29:22,200
Don't overthink it.

400
00:29:24,620 --> 00:29:26,500
Let's just get this over with.

401
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:31,060
Of course, it shouldn't
take long after all.

402
00:29:53,260 --> 00:29:56,240
We don't need this
unpleasantness to drag on.

403
00:29:58,340 --> 00:30:02,220
We know you're connected to
Straw Hat, so start talking.

404
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:11,120
Why have you come to the land of Wano?

405
00:30:11,520 --> 00:30:12,814
What are you plotting?

406
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:16,720
I want every last detail.

407
00:30:26,980 --> 00:30:28,380
Wow.
